Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||05-24-2001||08:31 PM||||I have the electronic type Accel coil and have mounted it on the engine side of the trunk wall. Even after three years and thousands of miles I havn't had one problem with it! I think it has to do a lot with where you mount it.<BR>Even though mine is in a place where it should fry it keeps going,there must be some kind of air getting to it.<BR>I have seen and talked to other people that have mounted it there and they too have no problems.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
